{"title":"2006 iTest Problems/Problem 36","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/f/10f32377ac67d94f764f12a15ea987e88c85d3e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> denote <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/e/93e0aee76702897a7487d931f5fd4b1fd449144b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos^{-1}(\\tfrac 23)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"65\" height=\"21\" />. The recursive sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/7/7577dc84ba759df2186e9e9720462445fc293378.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_0,a_1,a_2,\\ldots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"95\" height=\"11\" /> satisfies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/4/ea47b324908b7a67b59b71b4cb31334dfb4fe943.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_0 = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"49\" height=\"14\" /> and, for all positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/e/20e6ddd1eccd3fbca107b5e30d09d31853ffd8a2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_n = \\dfrac{\\cos(n\\alpha) - (a_1a_{n-1} + \\cdots + a_{n-1}a_1)}{2a_0}.\\]\" width=\"318\" height=\"41\" /> Suppose that the series <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/3/7635d053b712054572e4fad8ed9e7f52d79e3036.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{k=0}^\\infty\\dfrac{a_k}{2^k}\\]\" width=\"48\" height=\"48\" /> can be expressed uniquely as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/4/e8483815cf73a9eb4deadb40a2513f4c3e0143bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac{p\\sqrt q}r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"26\" height=\"24\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> are coprime positive integers and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is not divisible by the square of any prime. Find the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/8/d08ff3681d6992f69ee41e21c7237c89f970ac49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p+q+r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"71\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_36&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We write <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/3/2a3553d10076897731cfb2ce3aeae11789de223f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{k=0}^n a_k a_{n-k} = \\cos(n\\alpha)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"166\" height=\"48\" /> by rearranging the defining equation and using <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/4/ea47b324908b7a67b59b71b4cb31334dfb4fe943.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_0 = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"49\" height=\"14\" />. Summing this with weights <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/9/6a9d673d65890159f1b96de58534ace88e116671.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2^n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" /> from zero to infinity, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/f/90f1c8f8ae7f7b2adb96fbc2ac9649f88c7cf6a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{n=0}^{\\infty}\\frac{1}{2^n}\\sum_{n}^{k=0} a_k a_{n-k} = \\sum_{n=0}^{\\infty} \\frac{\\cos(n\\alpha)}{2^n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"253\" height=\"51\" />. We can rewrite this as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/8/178f2ba76366d0ae057d36cbda9d2ce4bb1546ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\sum_{n=0}^{\\infty} \\frac{a_n}{2^n})^2 = \\sum_{n=0}^{\\infty} \\frac{\\cos(n\\alpha)}{2^n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"189\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p><p>Next, we compute<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/1/2a12dc902dee5d95fd7b60f93eb003b3fd183bf2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{n=0}^{\\infty} \\frac{\\cos(n\\alpha)}{2^n} = \\frac{1}{2}(\\sum_{n=0}^{\\infty} \\frac{e^{in\\alpha}}{2^n} + \\sum_{n=0}^{\\infty} \\frac{e^{-in\\alpha}}{2^n}) = \\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{1}{1-\\frac{e^{i\\alpha}}{2}} + \\frac{1}{1-\\frac{e^{-i\\alpha}}{2}})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"503\" height=\"48\" />, which simplifies to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/2/c92280f11aed9c3a52547e04928d2a7aec4d07ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1 - \\frac{e^{i\\alpha} + e^{-i\\alpha}}{4}}{\\frac{5}{4} - \\frac{e^{i\\alpha} + e^{-i\\alpha}}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"96\" height=\"51\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/d/6cd4845f0518481bd1f194aa434aeb43084d57f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{e^{i\\alpha} + e^{-i\\alpha}}{2} = \\cos\\alpha = \\frac{2}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"181\" height=\"39\" />, the entire expression becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/1/7213dc20780e4a9ece1e6f4aaf1ffd011f528dc3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1 - \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot\\frac{2}{3}}{\\frac{5}{4} - \\frac{2}{3}} = \\frac{\\frac{2}{3}}{\\frac{7}{12}} = \\frac{8}{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"151\" height=\"47\" />.\n</p><p>Taking square roots, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/b/03bc556d236381d5bf0864079f47373cbdb3fbc0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{n=0}^{\\infty} \\frac{a_n}{2^n} = \\sqrt{\\frac{8}{7}} = \\frac{2\\sqrt{14}}{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"175\" height=\"49\" />, so our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/a/c4adf42afb3594e1fb1196b2d38e2b64b805d5db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 + 14 + 7 = \\boxed{23}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"135\" height=\"23\" /> and we are done.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_36&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest\" title=\"2006 iTest\">2006 iTest</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems\" title=\"2006 iTest Problems\">(Problems</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2006 iTest Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key)</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by:<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_35\" title=\"2006 iTest Problems/Problem 35\">Problem 35</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by:<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_37\" title=\"2006 iTest Problems/Problem 37\">Problem 37</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2006 iTest Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2006 iTest Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_3